    "body": "## Reopened — no-deletion doctrine\n\nReframing this from \"closed as stale\" to \"open as tracked work.\"\n\n**Status (Sept 22, 2026)**:\n- `canon-md` branch still exists in this repo (verified via API)\n- `CANON.md` exists on both main and canon-md branches\n- The Tier-1 lint coverage may or may not still flag this — re-run needed\n\nPer Casey Digennaro's no-deletion doctrine (filed in canon as `doctrine-no-deletion-2026-09-22`), we don't close canon-tracking issues as stale. We leave them open and tracked until the actual workflow is resolved (merge canon-md → main, or confirm content is already equivalent).\n\n**Action items**:\n1. Re-run `fleet-canon/lint.py` against current main to confirm coverage state\n2. If still flagging: merge canon-md or cherry-pick CANON.md (preferred)\n3. If resolved: this issue can be re-closed with concrete evidence, not \"stale\"\n\nPer doctrine: status checks are not closures. Reopening.",
